{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im","id":998515,"title":"Questions about Wasu-im","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-04T17:33:50-07:00","id":998515,"title":"Questions about Wasu-im","content":"Hello, i am reading the description of Death Rage.<br /> <br /> First is the triggers, does a character has to choose only the set of triggers in the sidebar of page 103? Can they mix them up? Say<br /> Passive: your auspice moon in the sky.<br /> Common: seeing someone attack a member of your pack.<br /> Specific: you swallow human blood.<br /> <br /> And the second question is about getting away from triggers. PC encounters a trigger, then he can roll composure + resolve to get away but them it gets confusing on how when the werewolf comes back say in the next scene or same if he rolled an exceptional success if he get triggered again.<br /> <br /> How do you get away from certain triggers? Say watching your moon in the sky (common), the pc rolls get indoors and then cames back but the moon still there so he has to roll again in a vicious circle or play agoraphobic for the rest of the session?<br /> <br /> Same for other triggers that seem limiting in the kind of game one can play. If someone picks &quot;the other&quot; then dealing with vampires or other supernaturals is out of the question because bob is gonna flip his shit everytime jerry the vampire uses a discipline for the 5th time.<br /> <br /> At first i though that i read that one could only be triggered once per session but i seem to have missread that somewhere. As written it seem a little problematic to say to a player &quot;oh sorry your character moon is on the sky this session go play the xbox&quot;<br /> <br /> So my question boils down to &quot;if one gets away from their trigger, vents ones rage and comes back and find the same trigger again, does he get triggered again&quot;?<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T18:01:38-07:00","id":998526,"title":"","content":"You can mix up the triggers, but by design you're meant to pick a group of them.<br /> <br /> If a PC encounters a trigger, they can roll Composure + Resolve to get a turn of lucidity. If you use that turn to get away, then come back to the trigger, you're going to get triggered again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How do you get away from certain triggers? Say watching your moon in the sky (common), the pc rolls get indoors and then cames back but the moon still there so he has to roll again in a vicious circle or play agoraphobic for the rest of the session? </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's why disharmony can be a bad thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Same for other triggers that seem limiting in the kind of game one can play. If someone picks &quot;the other&quot; then dealing with vampires or other supernaturals is out of the question because bob is gonna flip his shit everytime jerry the vampire uses a discipline for the 5th time. </div> </div> </div>Well dealing with vampires or other supernaturals isn't out of the question. It just limits the way you will be dealing with other supernaturals, especially if you tend towards extreme ends of Harmony.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At first i though that i read that one could only be triggered once per session but i seem to have missread that somewhere. As written it seem a little problematic to say to a player &quot;oh sorry your character moon is on the sky this session go play the xbox&quot; </div> </div> </div>No limit to that. There are ways to help resist rage. It's probably worth noting that the rhythm of the moon is not constrained by the tides in your game. Your Storyteller has your character sheet, or has seen it, and if he's chosen the moon that triggers you to shine overhead during a scene, it's for a reason. At least it should be. Just like a werewolf player who wants their character to have a torrid romance with a vampire and be best friends with a mage should not be picking the Other trigger for their character unless they purposely want those relationships to potentially lead to death.<br /> <br /> Yes they get triggered again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-04-2016, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T18:15:27-07:00","id":998533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998526#post998526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that's why disharmony can be a bad thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>But watching your auspice moon in the sky is a common trigger not a passive one. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998526#post998526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No limit to that. There are ways to help resist rage. It's probably worth noting that the rhythm of the moon is not constrained by the tides in your game. Your Storyteller has your character sheet, or has seen it, and if he's chosen the moon that triggers you to shine overhead during a scene, it's for a reason. At least it should be. Just like a werewolf player who wants their character to have a torrid romance with a vampire and be best friends with a mage should not be picking the Other trigger for their character unless they purposely want those relationships to potentially lead to death.<br /> <br /> Yes they get triggered again.</div> </div> </div> </div>We usually roll a d10 to decide which moon the game starts in for the essence so who get the free point is fair. But as written the common trigger seem too limiting to gameplay to me and my group so good to know i wasnt missreading so i can remove the rule or houserule it for once per session or handle it narratively.<br /> <br /> If they pick taint then its all punch wounds and no other interactions outside of combat same with the &quot;other&quot;, the pack means all combat is gonna escalate or in any kind of physical duel one of the pc is gonna have to be away and combat will always result in death rage as taking garu is authomatic death rage while in wasu-im.<br /> <br /> Moon means 2/10 chance everygame of a character not playing or playing the agoraphobic. So or everyone picks blood or the game becomes a cascade of nopes<br /> <br /> Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 11-04-2016, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T18:22:39-07:00","id":998537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998533#post998533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But watching your auspice moon in the sky is a common trigger not a passive one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Common Triggers happen at Harmony 8 and 9 and 1 and 2. I'd consider it disharmonous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T18:27:36-07:00","id":998538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998537#post998537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Common Triggers happen at Harmony 8 and 9 and 1 and 2. I'd consider it disharmonous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh you are right, i though it was 8-7 for common, still not working for my group they all started freshly change werewolves at harmony 8, not really looking for them to miss a big chunks of the game because of the triggers they picked and didnt knew how limiting they were at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T19:03:52-07:00","id":998554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998538#post998538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uh you are right, i though it was 8-7 for common, still not working for my group they all started freshly change werewolves at harmony 8, not really looking for them to miss a big chunks of the game because of the triggers they picked and didnt knew how limiting they were at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the design of Harmony is that it'll move a bit more often than I think you expect. If you're kicking things off at Harmony 8, I would advise that you give them early and often opportunities to Break Towards Spirit. At Harmony 8, there are 4 more breaking points that are great as &quot;I'm a new Werewolf; how does everything work?&quot; In particular, &quot;Inflicting Lunacy on a loved one&quot; is a great illustration of basic monstrosity and a good story hook about the novelty of the Uratha experience, and acts as a decent counterpoint to a Kuruth trigger problem.<br /> <br /> I think that anticipating that the first session or two, depending on your pace, will be mildly frustrating and explaining to your players that this is a &quot;your characters are newbies and learning the ropes&quot; might be enough to deal with the problem.<br /> <br /> Also, Harmony shouldn't be static. At all. If none of the characters change their Harmony stat in a session, I'd be asking why. Maybe they're rolling stupidly good, but more likely it's just a lack of opportunity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T20:02:14-07:00","id":998582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998554#post998554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the design of Harmony is that it'll move a bit more often than I think you expect. If you're kicking things off at Harmony 8, I would advise that you give them early and often opportunities to Break Towards Spirit. At Harmony 8, there are 4 more breaking points that are great as &quot;I'm a new Werewolf; how does everything work?&quot; In particular, &quot;Inflicting Lunacy on a loved one&quot; is a great illustration of basic monstrosity and a good story hook about the novelty of the Uratha experience, and acts as a decent counterpoint to a Kuruth trigger problem.<br /> <br /> Also, Harmony shouldn't be static. At all. If none of the characters change their Harmony stat in a session, I'd be asking why. Maybe they're rolling stupidly good, but more likely it's just a lack of opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Inflicting lunacy on a love one seem shitty to me, basically i am taking an NPC the player created and inmediately take him away in 3 sessions by forcing the issue. So thats a no.<br /> <br /> We are currently in session 3, they got to hunt a spirit as part of a small &quot;rite of passage&quot; and now they got the basic tribes explained to them. Noone move from 8 yet.<br /> <br /> Personally i dont like forcing things, if they drop they drop or raise i dont particularly like to engineer scenarios in which &quot;either you risk disharmony or something awful happens&quot; i prefer &quot;There is this situations and one of the options is a harmony dropping/raising one&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998554#post998554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that anticipating that the first session or two, depending on your pace, will be mildly frustrating and explaining to your players that this is a &quot;your characters are newbies and learning the ropes&quot; might be enough to deal with the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well my players are newbies-ish thats why we started as newly changed because chargen assumed every single player read the book and overwhelms them with choices so we just started with 1 gift and auspice as newly changed. But i think you missing the point of my issue, the fact that this loops on trigger or burn bridges as far as stories i can tell happen with the rules as written means they arent good fit for me and my group.<br /> <br /> The players and me just though that maybe 1 per session there was a risk to kuruth and that was fine. But as written means that several plot lines will not work.<br /> <br /> &quot;X player pick &quot;other&quot; as trigger, i guess he wont be participating in the plotline with vampires unless is full combat&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Z player pick &quot;pack&quot;, so i guess he wont enter combat with the rest&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Y player pick the moon, opps the dice rolled his moon hope he enjoys the essence he wont be able to spend this game because he wont be able to walk outside&quot;<br /> <br /> Fluff wise i like the idea that certain thing can trigger the PC to rage but as written they seem unnecessary restrictive to the participation of the players or a big chunk of the game in general.<br /> <br /> Maybe i will dig the 1st edition rules for kuruth or just make as each trigger can only be triggered once per session or just drop the whole &quot;Passive/common/specific&quot; trigger mechanic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T20:45:09-07:00","id":998592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998582#post998582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inflicting lunacy on a love one seem shitty to me, basically i am taking an NPC the player created and inmediately take him away in 3 sessions by forcing the issue. So thats a no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, if that's the absolute only way you could possibly do that, then I guess it's too bad you've restricted yourself in that way. I do appreciate that out of every single PC you have, they each only have a single possible loved one and that the only possible way for Lunacy to affect that person is for them to be removed from play. That seems like a <i>lot</i> of burned bridges in terms of story potential.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998582#post998582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are currently in session 3, they got to hunt a spirit as part of a small &quot;rite of passage&quot; and now they got the basic tribes explained to them. Noone move from 8 yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you have them perform a Siskur-Dah? If so, who led it? Why didn't that person get a breaking point?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998582#post998582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally i dont like forcing things, if they drop they drop or raise i dont particularly like to engineer scenarios in which &quot;either you risk disharmony or something awful happens&quot; i prefer &quot;There is this situations and one of the options is a harmony dropping/raising one&quot;<br /> <br /> But i think you missing the point of my issue, the fact that this loops on trigger or burn bridges as far as stories i can tell happen with the rules as written means they arent good fit for me and my group.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've engineered a scenario that's basically contrary to the rules and consequently, the rules don't work for you. This is not surprising. You want your PCs to live at Harmony 8 with no significant consequences. This is not how the game is designed. You are supposed to be slipping between 4 and 6, and maybe occasionally slide to 3 or 7. If you're playing at a static Harmony 8, then you are deliberately exploring the consequences of disharmony and Kuruth risk.<br /> <br /> A new Werewolf is, indeed, at an increased risk of Kuruth. That's supposed to express the horror of an ignorant Werewolf who doesn't understand the consequences of being imbalanced towards the Flesh. It's supposed to be a horrific thing. But with guidance, the <i>first thing they should be taught</i> is to move their Harmony down towards 5 by doing things that help balance them out. Because other Werewolves don't want you to lose control constantly. So they teach Harmony, how to balance the two sides of their lives in relatively equal portion.<br /> <br /> If you really need to hack the rules such that you have a <b>worse than the recommended start</b>, then yeah, you should absolutely hack it again and lighten the Kuruth triggers.<br /> <br /> Again: if you start play at Harmony 8, you are making it harder on your players. If you, and your players, are as newbie as you claim, <i>why did you do that</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T22:39:10-07:00","id":998622,"title":"","content":"Here's the deal. You made the choice of playing just-turned werewolves. If you've seen any werewolf media at all, you should know what life is like for just-turned werewolves. It's not that if you roll the wrong moon phase Steve's player has to out this session. It's that if you roll the right moon phase, this session is going to be about trying to keep Steve restrained so he doesn't Wolf out and eat someone, and/or running damage control in the aftermath of Steve's feeding frenzy. That's what playing a just-turned Werewolf <i>should</i> feel like, and that's <i>why</i> just-turned werewolves drink the kool-aid when more experienced wolves offer to teach them to control their rage. If you didn't want to play a story about muddling through the early nights of werewolfhood, you should have played with characters who have already figured that shit out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-05-2016, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T05:32:05-07:00","id":998711,"title":"","content":"Also, Kuruth triggers do not force a low-level characters player to sit out an entire session. It only lasts 10 minutes at primal urge 1 and 2. And also I'm pretty sure one of the devs/writers said you only get personal triggers dinged once per night or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T06:03:32-07:00","id":998715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998592#post998592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you have them perform a Siskur-Dah? If so, who led it? Why didn't that person get a breaking point?</div> </div> </div> </div>He passed that roll. As for the rest, a mock hunt for a spirit doesnt really offer much opportunities to most of the breaking point toward spirits.<br /> <br /> Killing a human and wolf (wrong type of hunt)<br /> Cannibalism.<br /> Killing a packmate.<br /> Staying a month in the hisil. Or staying 1 day. (Neither happened because of quick thinking and they pulling some good ideas)<br /> And staying away from their pack for more than 2 days. (Which they werent a pack yet at the time so no)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998592#post998592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've engineered a scenario that's basically contrary to the rules and consequently, the rules don't work for you. This is not surprising. You want your PCs to live at Harmony 8 with no significant consequences. This is not how the game is designed. You are supposed to be slipping between 4 and 6, and maybe occasionally slide to 3 or 7. If you're playing at a static Harmony 8, then you are deliberately exploring the consequences of disharmony and Kuruth risk.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean <b><u>some </u></b>consequence not the massive consequences that are the kuruth triggers. That once per session the threat of kuruth triggers are there? I am fine with that. Shapeshifting takes too long? I am fine. They got problems to access the shadow? i am fine. The way kuruth is apparently written, not for me.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998592#post998592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again: if you start play at Harmony 8, you are making it harder on your players. If you, and your players, are as newbie as you claim, <i>why did you do that</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not a newbie to the game i ran the shit of Forsaken 1st. However the players are 1 person who is new to WoD games, another who play some but dont remember much and another who wont ever touch a rulebook. I mostly choose 8 because newly changed i read, i think it was on some thread or book, that a newly change started at 9. But that seem too punitive so i moved it to 8 so the harder part i had in mind was the difficulty in shapeshifting (taking an action) and problem moving to the Shadow.<br /> <br /> And you are not really making a case for kuruth triggers because your only argument so far is. &quot;Harmony should drop or raise fast so you can ignore triggers&quot; so if the only defense for the mechanic is &quot;i can eventually ignore it&quot; then why i dont cut the middle man and ignore it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998622#post998622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not that if you roll the wrong moon phase Steve's player has to out this session. It's that if you roll the right moon phase, this session is going to be about trying to keep Steve restrained so he doesn't Wolf out and eat someone, and/or running damage control in the aftermath of Steve's feeding frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that is not really that isnt it? In Steve moon, steve should be put in a box/sealed room and left there with little to no risk of kuruth because there is no way to be outside at night and not see the moon (or better put, is tricky to handle that on table top. What Comp + Resolv roll every turn to see if you watch the moon While outside?). So staying in a close room is a perfect solution that is both quick and shit to the player who plays steve but is the one that makes the most sense IC. I dont see much drama and excitement in something that has such an easy solution that at the same time removes a player from playing.<br /> <br /> Steve has the moon trigger. Steve goes to his room for the rest of the session. Why restraining? If the trigger makes kuruth happen there is not much restraining to do consider an elodoth can cancel it or if not the rest of the pack has to get away or get infected so your scenario is kind of false.<br /> <br /> I have played high rage character in WtA and they can be interesting. How in your moon using the steve example, everything is more of a trigger to Frenzy and the pack has to calm you down etc etc. But as written here? There is no calming down, either this trigger you and you run away/smash it or it doesnt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998622#post998622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what playing a just-turned Werewolf <i>should</i> feel like, and that's <i>why</i> just-turned werewolves drink the kool-aid when more experienced wolves offer to teach them to control their rage. If you didn't want to play a story about muddling through the early nights of werewolfhood, you should have played with characters who have already figured that shit out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or i could just wanted to make getting gifts, rites and a tribe something organic? Which i did. And there is no way aside from certain gifts and the basic mechanic of harmony to &quot;teach werewolf&quot; to control their rage. There is only &quot;ok, dont be near your triggers&quot; and &quot;pay xp for this gifts&quot; and thats about it.<br /> <br /> Honestly there isnt much to discuss here. I saw the way kuruth triggers are written, ask for confirmation if i understood the rules okay. Apparently I did and they dont bring anything good to <b><u>my</u></b> table as they are written. I consider them too restrictive to gameplay and neither you nor <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2758\" data-vbnamecard=\"2758\">Errol216</a> are bringing up how that is not. Instead you are just arguing that they can be ignore because of the mobility of harmony, which kinda begs the question as to why then not just remove them? And incorrect information/missing the point like &quot;when your trigger is up either derail the whole game to deal with it with the rest of the pack has to restrain you when it happens (which they can because they can be infected by kuruth), before it happens (which is stupidly easy but leave a Player out of the game) or do clean up for what they did.<br /> <br /> Neither option i consider fun nor that bring anything interesting to the table i can do better narratively. So you are barking at the wrong tree here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998711#post998711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Kuruth triggers do not force a low-level characters player to sit out an entire session. It only lasts 10 minutes at primal urge 1 and 2. And also I'm pretty sure one of the devs/writers said you only get personal triggers dinged once per night or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats what i though but apparently is not like that. Say you got moon as your trigger, you watch your moon and succeed on the composure roll and get away and vent your fury but then you came back to the pack and see your moon again (because as you said, 10 minutes, the moon inst going anywhere) and then get trigger again, rinse and repeat. I wouldn't mind if, as you said, it was once per session or night even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 11-05-2016, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T06:45:06-07:00","id":998732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998715#post998715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thats what i though but apparently is not like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoever told you that was just flat out wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf the Forsaken Second edition, page 103</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each werewolf has a set of Kuruth triggers that apply<br /> just to him. Which trigger affects him at any given time<br /> depends on his Harmony. A player should pick one of the<br /> following sets of triggers so she knows what will affect her<br /> character when his Harmony changes. Werewolves also<br /> have general triggers, events that will push any werewolf<br /> into Death Rage. All of the general triggers affect every<br /> werewolf; though<b> she only suffers her personal triggers<br /> once a night</b>, general triggers have no such limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T06:49:45-07:00","id":998734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998715#post998715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that is not really that isnt it? In Steve moon, steve should be put in a box/sealed room and left there with little to no risk of kuruth because there is no way to be outside at night and not see the moon (or better put, is tricky to handle that on table top. What Comp + Resolv roll every turn to see if you watch the moon While outside?). So staying in a close room is a perfect solution that is both quick and shit to the player who plays steve but is the one that makes the most sense IC. I dont see much drama and excitement in something that has such an easy solution that at the same time removes a player from playing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why you <i>give Steve a reason to want to leave the room</i>. Put his Touchstone in danger. Or have some spirit come in and harass him. If being forced to stay locked in a room all night isn't dramatic it's because the Storyteller isn't providing the scenario with a source of conflict.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998715#post998715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Steve has the moon trigger. Steve goes to his room for the rest of the session. Why restraining? If the trigger makes kuruth happen there is not much restraining to do consider an elodoth can cancel it or if not the rest of the pack has to get away or get infected so your scenario is kind of false.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rest of the pack should be trying to keep him safe. That might mean convincing him not to go try to save his Touchstone. It might mean protecting his saferoom from the Pure that want to drag him outside and show him the moon. Or, it might mean making plans to get him where he needs to go without losing it. Do a Chain Rage Rite, or blindfold him until you can get him to the enemy's territory and set him loose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998715#post998715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have played high rage character in WtA and they can be interesting. How in your moon using the steve example, everything is more of a trigger to Frenzy and the pack has to calm you down etc etc. But as written here? There is no calming down, either this trigger you and you run away/smash it or it doesnt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure there is. There are rites that can stave off the rage. You can craft fetishes to help calm your rage, or barter for them if no one knows how to craft them yet. If you have an Elodoth you can give them some lucidity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998715#post998715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or i could just wanted to make getting gifts, rites and a tribe something organic? Which i did. And there is no way aside from certain gifts and the basic mechanic of harmony to &amp;quot;teach werewolf&amp;quot; to control their rage. There is only &amp;quot;ok, dont be near your triggers&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;pay xp for this gifts&amp;quot; and thats about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, cue boromir saying &quot;one does not simply pay xp for a gift.&quot; You actually have to have them carved into your soul, which means convincing a spirit to do carve it for you. It's not a simple process. Second of all, what the experienced werewolves are going to teach you is that you have to balance your harmony to make it easier to resist Kuruth, and they will show you how to balance your harmony. They can also teach you rites like Chain Rage that can help in other ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T06:50:53-07:00","id":998735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998732#post998732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whoever told you that was just flat out wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice, i miss that part i was reading through the Wasu-im section but miss the end of the trigger sidebar. Glad to know i was understanding the Wasu-im wrong and there is not a loop with the triggers.<br /> <br /> Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T07:13:06-07:00","id":998745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998734#post998734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why you <i>give Steve a reason to want to leave the room</i>. Put his Touchstone in danger. Or have some spirit come in and harass him. If being forced to stay locked in a room all night isn't dramatic it's because the Storyteller isn't providing the scenario with a source of conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or as i pointed out before i dont like to force conflict to &quot;either you enter kuruth or something awful happens&quot; scenarios. If you like that kind of forced narrative &quot;woe is me&quot; then good for you. I dont, i think is incredible dull, cliche and frankly unorganic. It just happen your touchstone is in danger on the moon your trigger is on? And the only way is to save them is to risk it? Cliche, incredibly cliche. Spiderman is not as predictable when he abandons his spiderman persona.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998734#post998734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rest of the pack should be trying to keep him safe. That might mean convincing him not to go try to save his Touchstone. It might mean protecting his saferoom from the Pure that want to drag him outside and show him the moon. Or, it might mean making plans to get him where he needs to go without losing it. Do a Chain Rage Rite, or blindfold him until you can get him to the enemy's territory and set him loose.</div> </div> </div> </div>The player would confine his PC himself first in most cases. If the pure is gonna come knocking on his moon (assuming they know his trigger) and then forcing him to kuruth..... that seem incredible suicidal from the part of the pure but whatever. And the last one, sure it could work but it seem too much work for little gain in the narrative sense.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998734#post998734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, cue boromir saying &quot;one does not simply pay xp for a gift.&quot; You actually have to have them carved into your soul, which means convincing a spirit to do carve it for you. It's not a simple process. Second of all, what the experienced werewolves are going to teach you is that you have to balance your harmony to make it easier to resist Kuruth, and they will show you how to balance your harmony. They can also teach you rites like Chain Rage that can help in other ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>What the hell does how you get a gift matters in this discussion? I just said, i prefer for them to gain each gift organically (meaning the whole crafting into your soul) instead of starting with a few, was one of the reason for newly change werewolves. You mean when i said the tribes teach gifts? I mean that they can tell the werewolf of the existence of certain gift that help with the fury.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T07:35:50-07:00","id":998752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998745#post998745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or as i pointed out before i dont like to force conflict to &amp;quot;either you enter kuruth or something awful happens&amp;quot; scenarios. If you like that kind of forced narrative &amp;quot;woe is me&amp;quot; then good for you. I dont, i think is incredible dull, cliche and frankly unorganic.</div> </div> </div> </div>What sort of conflict <i>do</i> you like? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998745#post998745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just happen your touchstone is in danger on the moon your trigger is on?</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you ever seen or read anything with werewolves in it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998745#post998745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the only way is to save them is to risk it?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's up to the players to decide. It's the Storyteller's job to pose dramatic questions and the players' job to answer them. If they come up with a way to save Steve's Touchstone without Steve falling into Kuruth, good for them. The fact that Steve being at risk of death raging forced them to make a choice and come up with a plan means it did its job. It generated conflict.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998745#post998745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cliche, incredibly cliche.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please don't insult my taste in stories.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998745#post998745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spiderman is not as predictable when he abandons his spiderman persona.</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm... what?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998745#post998745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The player would confine his PC himself first in most cases. If the pure is gonna come knocking on his moon (assuming they know his trigger) and then forcing him to kuruth..... that seem incredible suicidal from the part of the pure but whatever. And the last one, sure it could work but it seem too much work for little gain in the narrative sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. These are all potential answers to the dramatic question posed by Steve being unable to leave the basement without risking death rage. Resolving these conflicts is how stories are made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998745#post998745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the hell does how you get a gift matters in this discussion? I just said, i prefer for them to gain each gift organically (meaning the whole crafting into your soul) instead of starting with a few, was one of the reason for newly change werewolves. You mean when i said the tribes teach gifts? I mean that they can tell the werewolf of the existence of certain gift that help with the fury.</div> </div> </div> </div>You said &quot;there is no way aside from certain gifts and the basic mechanic of harmony to &amp;quot;teach werewolf&amp;quot; to control their rage. There is only 'ok, dont be near your triggers' and 'pay xp for this gifts' and thats about it.&quot; I was just pointing out that &quot;pay xp for these gifts&quot; is not as simple as you were making it out to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T07:49:35-07:00","id":998764,"title":"","content":"If it's a choice between cliche and one of your players sitting in a basement all session, I'd pick the option that actually leads to a story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T10:05:32-07:00","id":998803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998715#post998715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the rest, a mock hunt for a spirit doesnt really offer much opportunities to most of the breaking point toward spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>W:tF 2e, p104</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The breaking points below apply to all Uratha. They\u2019re a starting point rather than a definitive list. The player and Storyteller should work together to define one or two breaking points in each direction for her character based on her auspice, tribe, and Touchstones. Breaking points toward Flesh involve actively denying her Uratha nature. Breaking points toward Spirit instead require her to turn her back on her heritage in the world of Flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>You did that, right? Because actually doing that is a great exercise for <i>actually understanding the game</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998715#post998715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you are not really making a case for kuruth triggers because your only argument so far is. &quot;Harmony should drop or raise fast so you can ignore triggers&quot; so if the only defense for the mechanic is &quot;i can eventually ignore it&quot; then why i dont cut the middle man and ignore it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not trying to defend the game. I'm trying to explain to you how the game works, because you've demonstrated that you don't know how it works.<br /> <br /> If you ignore Kuruth triggers, then you've removed a large chunk of why Harmony exists as a mechanic at all. Not all of it, but the vast majority of it.<br /> <br /> My argument is that you shot yourself in the foot and now you're complaining about it, so <i>maybe</i> you shouldn't have shot yourself in the foot. Newly changed Werewolves are at higher risk of Kuruth because they're inexperienced and don't have any idea what their triggers are. This is not a situation for newbie <i>players</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Again</b>, if you don't want to play the game RAW, that's fine. But stop whining that the rules don't suit you if you're not going to use them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T10:07:14-07:00","id":998804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998745#post998745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont, i think is incredible dull, cliche and frankly unorganic. It just happen your touchstone is in danger on the moon your trigger is on? And the only way is to save them is to risk it? Cliche, incredibly cliche. Spiderman is not as predictable when he abandons his spiderman persona.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone who writes a story trying to avoid cliches is a terrible writer. Stop being impressed with your own originality and try telling a good story for once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T10:13:57-07:00","id":998807,"title":"","content":"I was wrong about personal triggers, for that I am sorry. It was right there at the bottom of the page.<br /> <br /> You are free to run the game the way you want, but a lot of your problems with the game seem to be due to misunderstandings, at least one due to me.<br /> <br /> For one thing you said inflicting Lunacy on a loved one is 'shitty.' Yes, it's not a nice thing to do, but when someone turns into a werewolf why wouldn't they show their loved one they can now shapeshift, heal faster, no longer need glasses, and so forth. Depending on how close the loved one is, it makes sense that they might notice the PC has had a sudden shift in their life. You also said that it takes them away in three sessions, but Lunacy doesn't just get rid of people, except in the way that could lead to a story.<br /> <br /> Another thing, you keep saying things don't feel organic, while simultaneously offering up clearly 'inorganic' structure. Rolling dice to determine what moon is in the sky, for instance, rather than having a period of time pass. If it's around a month, everyone's gotten 1 Essence back.<br /> <br /> And overall your complaints about Kuruth, again I admit some are due to my telling you incorrect rules, are overstated. Kuruth does not take people and situations out of play except at extreme ends of Harmony, instead it makes a situation more tense.<br /> <br /> Basically you're free to play the game you want, obviously, but some of your complaints about the game are unwarranted and only exist as complaints due to the way you're running it. They are not problems with the game, but with your houserules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-05-2016, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T10:26:02-07:00","id":998813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998804#post998804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone who writes a story trying to avoid cliches is a terrible writer. Stop being impressed with your own originality and try telling a good story for once.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">Please don't insult other people's writing.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T10:48:47-07:00","id":998816,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998803#post998803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Again</b>, if you don't want to play the game RAW, that's fine. But stop whining that the rules don't suit you if you're not going to use them.</div> </div> </div> </div>actually i was intending to houserule it to raw something that i miss read, you are defending a incorrect implementation of the rules that was corrected last page.<br /> <br /> And to be fair i didnt whine, i read the incorrect clarification, and this was my exact wordings<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998533#post998533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But as written the common trigger seem too limiting to gameplay to me and my group so good to know i wasnt missreading so i can remove the rule or houserule it for once per session or handle it narratively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Notice i said to &quot;me and my group&quot; and that i just wanted clarification if i understood the rules correctly? Even after you got all defensive on the mechanic and i told you that i wasnt interested and was just gonna remove it anyway you keep defending it. Even after i point out that for MY game it wasnt a good fit and was not interested in including it didnt have anything to offer.<br /> <br /> So what i said boils down to this.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998803#post998803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you ignore Kuruth triggers, then you've removed a large chunk of why Harmony exists as a mechanic at all. Not all of it, but the vast majority of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, i am aware of your opinion and i dont care. Shifting worlds, banes and shapeshifting is enough for me to justify harmony. Kuruth triggers is a useless cherry on the top of the harmony dessert <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u><b>to me.</b></u></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998807#post998807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wrong about personal triggers, for that I am sorry. It was right there at the bottom of the page.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries i miss that part too when i first read the book and that prompted this thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998807#post998807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And overall your complaints about Kuruth, again I admit some are due to my telling you incorrect rules, are overstated. Kuruth does not take people and situations out of play except at extreme ends of Harmony, instead it makes a situation more tense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, my original problem with kuruth trigger was the loop of &quot;PC sees the moon, wasu-im, goes away, vent his rages, comes back, sees the moon again, wasu-im again&quot; that either forces kuruth as inescapable or removes them form play. Limiting once per night is something i am cool with it but at the time i didnt found it when i read the wasu-im section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 11-05-2016, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T12:39:04-07:00","id":998859,"title":"","content":"As the book reads, your Harmony 8 Players have 30 seconds (ten turns) to snap out of Wasu-Im before they enter Basu-Im (which, at Primal Urge 1 or 2, lasts 10 minutes, and can be ended by and Elodoth, if they have one).While in Wasu-Im, the player can roll Resolve+Composure, each success giving him a turn which he controls himself and doesn't need to smash something to pieces. If he fails, he enters Basu-Im immediately.<br /> <br /> To avoid Basu-Im entirely, the player needs en Exceptional Success on the Resolve+Composure roll to resist. It can be very hard to achieve, specially since starting pools range from 7 to 9 dice, if you have Willpower to spend on it. However, a little bit of tweaking to the Social Maneuvering system gives some ways to help the character:<br /> <br /> Assuming his pack has at least an Average Impression with him, they can try to Force his doors and convince him to give it all when resisting Death Rage. Apply 1+Primal Urge as Doors. If the pack gets a success, you can give him a bonus to resit Death Rage (+1 for every success achieved, if they got 5 successes or more, add the Inspired Condition allowing for Exceptional Success on 3 instead of 5). However, if they fail, apply -1 to his resistance rolls, and if it was a Dramatic Fail, his next roll is reduced to a chance die.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, you might want to check the Pack Merit: Directed Rage, page 30 of <i>The Pack</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5446,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","user":"BinAly","date":". 11-05-2016, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T14:29:22-07:00","id":998888,"title":"","content":"At Harmony 8, your Common triggers are in play and you have to *Witness* your auspice moon in the sky. The character throws on a ball cap and keeps his head down whenever he goes outside. He resists looking up. The Storyteller might throw challenges his way, and his pack should help look out for him.<br /> <br /> He's a werewolf trying not to give into the moon's influence, knowing that it could put him and his loved ones in danger. IMO, this simulates most werewolf movies, and is the game working as it should. <br /> <br /> With Common triggers and vampires - you have to witness the vampire do something 'obviously inhuman'. So when the character (or pack) meets with the vampire, you tell her straight up that your moon's in the sky, you're feeling edgy, and if she tries to pull any vampire stuff you're going to lose your shit. That should help to keep the meeting civil, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T15:34:24-07:00","id":998912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998888#post998888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At Harmony 8, your Common triggers are in play and you have to *Witness* your auspice moon in the sky. The character throws on a ball cap and keeps his head down whenever he goes outside. He resists looking up. The Storyteller might throw challenges his way, and his pack should help look out for him.<br /> <br /> He's a werewolf trying not to give into the moon's influence, knowing that it could put him and his loved ones in danger. IMO, this simulates most werewolf movies, and is the game working as it should.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually we already clarified that is doesnt, <b><u>necessarily</u></b>, work that way. The PC could see the moon in the sky, enter a room, punch everything there thus venting his rage, and the spend the rest of the night watching his moon willy nilly with not problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T17:36:53-07:00","id":998959,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Please just stop with the contrary attitude, particularly when it is one of the game's writers giving a possible example of how a character with the trigger you spent over a page discussing could deal with said trigger. Bunyip did not say that was the only way to deal with the issue, so the comment about things not necessarily working that way is pedantic and borderline condescending. You are being argumentative for no reason, stop it.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T18:22:43-07:00","id":998972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998912#post998912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually we already clarified that is doesnt, <b><u>necessarily</u></b>, work that way. The PC could see the moon in the sky, enter a room, punch everything there thus venting his rage, and the spend the rest of the night watching his moon willy nilly with not problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, I was just trying to suggest ways that might appeal to you to incorporate it into your game, not get into a fight. However you want to run it is entirely up to you. I'm on record many times in this forum as supporting using the rules, but also encouraging everyone to go their own way if they want.<br /> <br /> Not anyone's enemy here. We're just looking to have fun from the game, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T19:53:44-07:00","id":999012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998972#post998972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, I was just trying to suggest ways that might appeal to you to incorporate it into your game, not get into a fight. However you want to run it is entirely up to you. I'm on record many times in this forum as supporting using the rules, but also encouraging everyone to go their own way if they want.<br /> <br /> Not anyone's enemy here. We're just looking to have fun from the game, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh i didnt meant to sound aggresive to you, more clarifying for errol tendency to flip, again my problem isnt with how to handle a 1 per night trigger but a barrage 24/7 loop of trigger by a missreading of the rules in which i though that you could get constantly triggered on the same night/day.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 11-05-2016, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T08:54:16-08:00","id":999242,"title":"","content":"Remaining on topic, I was re-reading the Wasu-Im rules, and found them a bit confusing:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Wasu-Im, the werewolf shifts immediately into Urshul or Dalu form and remains in that form for the duration. He suffers from a modified form of Gauru\u2019s Rage (p. 97). If he fails the Resolve + Composure roll for taking other actions, he enters Basu-Im.<br /> <br /> Instead of attacking, he can roll Resolve + Composure as an instant action to get some breathing room. Each success on the roll to resist offers him a turn of lucidity. If he rolls an exceptional success, he can end Wasu-Im. </div> </div> </div>Are those two different kinds of rolls, or is it the same test, and if I fail, I enter Basu-Im immediately? If they are the same, why not write the success and failure conditions on the same sentence? As written, it seems to point out two rolls:<br /> <br /> &quot;Gauru's Do something instead of attacking test&quot; and &quot;Wasu-Im's Get breathing room test&quot;.<br /> <br /> Edit: Right now, I'm rulling that you can roll for breathing room <i>while attacking</i>. To stop and do anything other than hurt people, you need the other roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T09:37:59-08:00","id":999265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=999242#post999242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are those two different kinds of rolls, or is it the same test, and if I fail, I enter Basu-Im immediately? If they are the same, why not write the success and failure conditions on the same sentence? As written, it seems to point out two rolls:</div> </div> </div> </div>One roll. In Wasu-Im, you can either (a) Attack or move to attack, or (b) roll Resolve + Compsure to do something else.<br /> <br /> If you choose to roll, you either (i) Fail, and enter Basu-Im, (ii) Succeed, and gain &lt; Success &gt; turns of doing other things, or (iii) Exceptionally Succeed, and leave Wasu-Im.<br /> <br /> Simple success doesn't end the count-down to Basu-Im. It just gives you time to prepare for Basu-Im, either by running away from your loved ones, locking yourself in a werewolf-proof cage, or moving to where you might bring the most hurt down on the enemy.<br /> <br /> Regarding your edit - Rolling for breathing room while attacking doesn't do anything. By attacking, you're doing what Wasu-Im wants, you're not buying any additional time. If you want to snap out of Wasu-Im you need to take a moment to stop and try and get yourself under control. Attacking doesn't do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T09:38:10-08:00","id":999266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=999242#post999242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remaining on topic, I was re-reading the Wasu-Im rules, and found them a bit confusing:<br /> <br /> Are those two different kinds of rolls, or is it the same test, and if I fail, I enter Basu-Im immediately? If they are the same, why not write the success and failure conditions on the same sentence? As written, it seems to point out two rolls:<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Gauru's Do something instead of attacking test&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;Wasu-Im's Get breathing room test&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Edit: Right now, I'm rulling that you can roll for breathing room <i>while attacking</i>. To stop and do anything other than hurt people, you need the other roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first paragraph refers to the Resolve + Composure roll that a werewolf in Gauru form (or the modified version of Gauru form's Rage ability) must make reflexively if they take any action other than attacking or moving closer to attack an active opponent. On a success nothing happens, on a failure you fall into Basu-Im. The second paragraph describes a separate Resolve + Composure roll you can make as an Instant action. On a success you get one turn per success rolled on which you can take actions other than attacking without have to make the roll referred to in the preceeding paragraph. On an exceptional success you come out of Wasu-Im, and on a failure you fall into Basu-Im.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T09:41:43-08:00","id":999268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=999265#post999265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One roll. In Wasu-Im, you can either (a) Attack or move to attack, or (b) roll Resolve + Compsure to do something else.<br /> <br /> If you choose to roll, you either (i) Fail, and enter Basu-Im, (ii) Succeed, and gain &lt; Success &gt; turns of doing other things, or (iii) Exceptionally Succeed, and leave Wasu-Im.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... You're the writer, so I'm sure you have a better grasp of the intent, but that's not how it reads to me. The first paragraph appears to be referring to the Rage ability of the Gauru form, which is reflexive and automatic if you do something other than attack, while the second paragraph appears to be describing a separate mechanic that allows you to intentionally take an instant action to attempt to gain multiple consecutive turns of not having to make the reflexive Resolve + Composure roll as described in the Gauru Rage mechanic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-06-2016, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T10:03:39-08:00","id":999280,"title":"","content":"It's entirely possible I'm wrong - it's been years now since we discussed and tested these rules. One of the design principles is to eliminate pointless or undramatic rolls. IMO, rolling Resolve+Composure just to see whether you can roll it again is a pointless roll.<br /> <br /> And this (as I believe) is why it's a modified form of Gauru's Rage - the same roll can give multiple turns of control, rather than a single turn-by-turn scenario.<br /> <br /> Another interpretation of the writing is that in Wasu-Im you can either (a) Attack, or (b) Rolle R+C to do something else. If you choose b, you can either do the one other action for one turn, or you can roll R+C again to see if you can continue to do something else for multiple turns. There's not much to gain by not going for multiple turns of control - you can always choose to fall into Basu-Im at any time. Essentially, you're just doubling up on rolls, which IMO is a less fun use of the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 11-06-2016, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T10:19:41-08:00","id":999293,"title":"","content":"Ah, I get it. The roll that gets you multiple turns of lucidity is an instant action, so you can't do anything else while you do it. <br /> <br /> So I think the intent is you either attack, do something else <i>that turn</i> and roll resolve+composure reflexively as if you were in gauru, <i>or</i> do nothing, roll resolve+composure as an instant action and get [sucess] turns of lucidity after that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T10:52:26-08:00","id":999313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=999293#post999293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I get it. The roll that gets you multiple turns of lucidity is an instant action, so you can't do anything else while you do it. <br /> <br /> So I think the intent is you either attack, do something else <i>that turn</i> and roll resolve+composure reflexively as if you were in gauru, <i>or</i> do nothing, roll resolve+composure as an instant action and get [sucess] turns of lucidity after that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my interpretation. Sorry if I didn't make that clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-06-2016, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T12:23:28-08:00","id":999369,"title":"","content":"I understood the rules as Charlaquin, two different actions. However, I agree on removal of pointless rolls, and I'm all for making them a single roll to do something <i>and</i> resist Wasu-Im, but as written, it doesn't seem like the intention was that.<br /> <br /> On the topic of boring rolls, I do believe that, as written, the system to snap out of Wasu-Im is pretty much forcing a ton of rolls without any meaningful impact. It is obvious that most of the time, Uratha will <i>not</i> want to lose control. A werewolf at Harmony 7 has 10 minutes to snap out out of Wasu-Im, which gives him 200 turns to keep on rolling to try and get an Exceptional Success...<br /> <br /> As I see it, the system would be better served by an extended roll, with the target being linked to Primal Urge, and the amount of rolls allowed being linked to Harmony, with a fixed interval... This way, at least you can build up the scene based on the progress, and apply conditions and things like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T14:20:41-08:00","id":999429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=999369#post999369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understood the rules as Charlaquin, two different actions. However, I agree on removal of pointless rolls, and I'm all for making them a single roll to do something <i>and</i> resist Wasu-Im, but as written, it doesn't seem like the intention was that.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, I wouldn't make both rolls on the same turn. The modified Gauru Rage roll happens if you want to do something besides attack <i>this turn</i>. The &quot;get some breathing room&quot; roll takes up your action on this turn and lets you spend the next few turns after this one making non-attack actions free of the modified Gauru Rage. By a highly technical reading, that would also mean you'd have to reflexively roll for Gauru Rage on the turn you try to get some breathing room, but I think that's pretty obviously not the intent. I would just say the turn you spend taking the &quot;get breathing room&quot; action doesn't trigger a reflexive Gauru Rage roll, or if you want to be a stickler for wording, at least count it as one of your turns of lucidity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=999369#post999369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the topic of boring rolls, I do believe that, as written, the system to snap out of Wasu-Im is pretty much forcing a ton of rolls without any meaningful impact. It is obvious that most of the time, Uratha will <i>not</i> want to lose control. A werewolf at Harmony 7 has 10 minutes to snap out out of Wasu-Im, which gives him 200 turns to keep on rolling to try and get an Exceptional Success...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the intent is that once you've fallen into Wasu-Im, you're <i>going</i> to go into Basu-Im, except in very rare cases. The point is you make that lucidity roll to buy yourself turns to get as far away as possible from anyone and anything you care about. Or failing that, to at least get into a position where you'll do more damage to your enemies than your allies. It's not Ook, you've got 200 tries to get an exceptional succcess&quot;, it's &quot;Ok, you've got three turns to try to position yourself, do you want to run away or try to get in the middle of the action?&quot; and for the chance of an exceptional success to be a lucky bonus. The 10 minutes probably won't all get played out in combat turns, at a certain point it becomes &quot;and after a few minutes of struggle, you finally succumb to full death rage. Fortunately since you were able to get a good distance into the woods, it's probably safe to assume you didn't cause too much collateral damage.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=999369#post999369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I see it, the system would be better served by an extended roll, with the target being linked to Primal Urge, and the amount of rolls allowed being linked to Harmony, with a fixed interval... This way, at least you can build up the scene based on the progress, and apply conditions and things like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be better if the goal was for pulling yourself out of Death Rage to be a matter of putting in enough effort over a period of time. But, I'm pretty sure the goal is to create a sense that &quot;resisting Death Rage&quot; is really just prolonging the inevitable. To allow for those moments of &quot;You know the man you truly are, Remus! This heart is where you truly live! This heart! Here! This flesh is only flesh!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-06-2016, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T16:10:52-08:00","id":999478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=999429#post999429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, I wouldn't make both rolls on the same turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, it really is better to avoid multiple rolls for the &quot;same&quot; result on the same turn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=999429#post999429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the intent is that once you've fallen into Wasu-Im, you're <i>going</i> to go into Basu-Im, except in very rare cases. The point is you make that lucidity roll to buy yourself turns to get as far away as possible from anyone and anything you care about. Or failing that, to at least get into a position where you'll do more damage to your enemies than your allies. It's not Ook, you've got 200 tries to get an exceptional succcess&quot;, it's &quot;Ok, you've got three turns to try to position yourself, do you want to run away or try to get in the middle of the action?&quot; and for the chance of an exceptional success to be a lucky bonus. The 10 minutes probably won't all get played out in combat turns, at a certain point it becomes &quot;and after a few minutes of struggle, you finally succumb to full death rage. Fortunately since you were able to get a good distance into the woods, it's probably safe to assume you didn't cause too much collateral damage.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I believe a single roll, at the moment of entering Wasu-Im, would be far better than the possibility of multiple rolls. Otherwise players might feel cheated if the Storyteller just blocks further chances to snap out of it by not allowing any more tests. Something like this:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Kuruth Trigger Reaction</b></span><br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Dicepool:</b> Resolve+Composure, penalized by the situation (for example, if in combat, it will be harder than if just glancing at the moon from a safe place)<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> Instantly enter Basu-Im, going straight for the source of the trigger. Even after Basu-Im ends, you suffer from the Atavism condition towards any sources of the same trigger.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> Enter Wasu-Im, suffering from the same Rage limitations from Gauru. After the Harmony timer expires, you enter Basu-Im.<br /> <b>Success:</b> Enter Wasu-Im, but do not suffer the Rage limitations from Gauru. However, each turn in the presence of the trigger forces a Resolve+Composure roll. On a failure on this roll, make when attack against the source. Willpower may be spent to avoid the attack automatically. If your character takes measures to avoid the trigger, he does not need to roll. Also, you react poorly to social interactions. Make the same Resolve+Composure roll whenever someone tries to interact with you, attacking once on a failure. After the Harmony timer expires, you enter Basu-Im.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> You lose the turn, but snap out of Wasu-Im an cannot suffer a Kuruth Trigger Reaction from the same trigger for the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Possible modifiers:</b> On your territory +1, Inside your Safe-Place/Den +Merit Rating, Rage will put a touchstone at risk +1, Trigger is abundant -1 to -3, Out of your territory -1, Enemies threatening touchstones -1<br /> <br /> With something like this, you can achieve the described intent without the need for pointless rolls, defining the tone of the scene in a single test.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=999429#post999429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That might be better if the goal was for pulling yourself out of Death Rage to be a matter of putting in enough effort over a period of time. But, I'm pretty sure the goal is to create a sense that &quot;resisting Death Rage&quot; is really just prolonging the inevitable. To allow for those moments of &quot;You know the man you truly are, Remus! This heart is where you truly live! This heart! Here! This flesh is only flesh!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Then something like what I described above would make sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T16:29:34-08:00","id":999487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=998711#post998711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Kuruth triggers do not force a low-level characters player to sit out an entire session. It only lasts 10 minutes at primal urge 1 and 2. And also I'm pretty sure one of the devs/writers said you only get personal triggers dinged once per night or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically, once you Kuruth, you're too spent for it to happen again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T16:47:31-08:00","id":999496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=999478#post999478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then I believe a single roll, at the moment of entering Wasu-Im, would be far better than the possibility of multiple rolls. Otherwise players might feel cheated if the Storyteller just blocks further chances to snap out of it by not allowing any more tests.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the rules are pretty clear on that, they shouldn't feel cheated if they've read them. The only way to break out of it is to get an Exceptional Success. Plus there's external abilities that assist these rolls. Chain Rage allows members of a pack to snap out of Wasu-Im if they make five turns of lucidity. Still Small Voice can be used on others in Wasu-Im to help them break out of it. The Controlled Burn Merit allows you to break out of it with a turn of lucidity and a Willpower.<br /> <br /> With your alternative idea, there's far less tension about the rage in general. It might be appropriate for games where people want to cut it out entirely. And attacking the source doesn't really fit, as the source is not always a tangible thing one can attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-06-2016, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T17:45:20-08:00","id":999500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=999429#post999429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, I wouldn't make both rolls on the same turn. The modified Gauru Rage roll happens if you want to do something besides attack <i>this turn</i>. The &quot;get some breathing room&quot; roll takes up your action on this turn and lets you spend the next few turns after this one making non-attack actions free of the modified Gauru Rage. By a highly technical reading, that would also mean you'd have to reflexively roll for Gauru Rage on the turn you try to get some breathing room, but I think that's pretty obviously not the intent. I would just say the turn you spend taking the &quot;get breathing room&quot; action doesn't trigger a reflexive Gauru Rage roll, or if you want to be a stickler for wording, at least count it as one of your turns of lucidity.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly what I was trying to say, although I was apparently not doing a good job of it.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't have the turn you spend catching your breath as one of your 'free' turns. I'd say the effort you've expended on your instant action justifies the count starting on the next turn. (Unless you fail and fall into Base-Im, of course.)<br /> <br /> That said, for the purposes of genre emulation, my opinion is that the intent is that when you are in Wasu-Im, you either attack or spend your instant action rolling R+C to give yourself more options in subsequent turns. This is different from the Gauru form Rage (hence 'modified') as in Wasu-Im you're no longer in complete control of yourself, whereas in (voluntarily taken, non-Kuruth) Gauru you have strong Rage-ly instincts to contend with, but you are actually in control. But if you do succeed in taking that one turn of fighting for control, you're able to 'ride the wave' and direct your actions as you want for a brief period.<br /> <br /> This instant action is that moment in every werewolf show where the werewolf fights the transformation and blood lust while her friends/onlookers stupidly stand there and ask if she's okay. Followed a few seconds later by her growling/screaming for them to run for their lives. (Which is also why Wasu-Im puts you in Dalu or Urshal, and not Gauru.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 11-06-2016, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T18:19:41-08:00","id":999511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=999500#post999500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is exactly what I was trying to say, although I was apparently not doing a good job of it.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't have the turn you spend catching your breath as one of your 'free' turns. I'd say the effort you've expended on your instant action justifies the count starting on the next turn. (Unless you fail and fall into Base-Im, of course.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we're on the same page on that part.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=999500#post999500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, for the purposes of genre emulation, my opinion is that the intent is that when you are in Wasu-Im, you either attack or spend your instant action rolling R+C to give yourself more options in subsequent turns. This is different from the Gauru form Rage (hence 'modified') as in Wasu-Im you're no longer in complete control of yourself, whereas in (voluntarily taken, non-Kuruth) Gauru you have strong Rage-ly instincts to contend with, but you are actually in control. But if you do succeed in taking that one turn of fighting for control, you're able to 'ride the wave' and direct your actions as you want for a brief period.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where we disagree. I don't think you've completely lost control yet in Wasu-Im; that's what Basu-Im is. Wasu-Im to me is the brief period where you're struggling to maintain control, but are fighting a losing battle. Also just from a phrasing perspective, I think the second of the paragraphs we're discussing completely explains the instant action R+C mechanic, obviating the need for mentioning the R+C roll for Gauru Rage in the preceeding paragraph.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=999500#post999500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This instant action is that moment in every werewolf show where the werewolf fights the transformation and blood lust while her friends/onlookers stupidly stand there and ask if she's okay. Followed a few seconds later by her growling/screaming for them to run for their lives. (Which is also why Wasu-Im puts you in Dalu or Urshal, and not Gauru.)</div> </div> </div> </div>In this, I agree 100%.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T19:10:53-08:00","id":999526,"title":"","content":"One might not always struggle in Wasu-Im.<br /> <br /> I see what Bunyip means, though.<br /> <br /> In Wasu-Im you can only fight or resist. Resisting doesn't allow you to do anything but potentially move, such as to a safer place to go berserk.<br /> <br /> In gauru form, you are urged, strongly, to fight. But if you want to do something else you have to roll Resolve + Composure to do it, not as an instant action. Meaning if I'm in gauru I have enough time to type in the password to my vault and throw myself in before going berserk. I can Reach through a Locus, use an ability to disable the enemy's silver weapon. Failure means Kuruth but it's still a potential action.<br /> <br /> Your control of what you can do in Wasu-Im is more limited than with gauru Rage. In a movie, it's when the guy is clutching his head, and his eyes have changed colors and he's either about to attack or run away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-06-2016, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T05:47:12-08:00","id":999687,"title":"","content":"Two things I am unsure about<b></b>:<br /> For Gauru rage: if you try to do something else than attacking or moving to attack in your limited turns of normal Gauru, it states that if you fail the roll, that you enter <i>Kuruth</i>. From what I undestand this means <i>Wasu-Im </i>not<i> Basu-Im </i>in this case. So you would shift down and have to deal with your death-rage. While if you already are in <i>Wasu-Im</i> and take the reflexive roll to do something else in the same turn, you risk falling into <i>Basu-Im</i> directly. Am I right about this?<br /> For <i>Wasu-Im</i>: if I take a turn to concentrate and give myself some breathing room (second paragraph roll), do I risk <i>Basu-Im</i> on failure as well? Because it is only explicitely stated for the reflexive roll. If so, this would make 200 consecutive roll for the exceptional succes very risky!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T06:02:31-08:00","id":999693,"title":"","content":"If you fall into Kuruth while in gauru, that's automatically Basu-Im. You just go berserk without any warning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T06:14:00-08:00","id":999697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=999687#post999687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For <i>Wasu-Im</i>: if I take a turn to concentrate and give myself some breathing room (second paragraph roll), do I risk <i>Basu-Im</i> on failure as well? Because it is only explicitely stated for the reflexive roll. If so, this would make 200 consecutive roll for the exceptional succes very risky!</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like you have to hit something if you fail that roll.<br /> <br /> But even if you keep getting turns of lucidity, without special help through aforementioned abilities or an Exceptional Success, Wasu-Im has a timer on the top of page 103. Assuming your turn lasts 3 seconds, at Harmony 4 and 6 you have, at most, a hundred turns. At 3 and 7 you have 20. At 4 and 8 10, 1 and 9 three, and 0 and 10 1. At that point if you haven't pulled yourself out of it you're going into Basu-Im, which Elfive points out is the full Kuruth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T06:28:40-08:00","id":999707,"title":"","content":"Not questioning, that it is kind of stupid and against the feel of werewolf to keep on rolling for control, instead of just trying to maintain control for a bit and use the time to get out of the way before <i>Basu-Im</i>, just wanted to know if it is even riskier than stated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=999693#post999693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you fall into Kuruth while in gauru, that's automatically Basu-Im. You just go berserk without any warning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you back this up by a quote or something? Because in the text it just says &quot;you fall into <i>Kuruth</i>&quot; which from the <i>Kuruth</i> section would mean <i>Wasu-Im</i> first. I kind of like both interpretations, just would like to make sure what the authors intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T06:34:25-08:00","id":999709,"title":"","content":"Sure, here you go, page 102:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Normally, a werewolf who encounters a<br /> Kuruth trigger enters Wasu-Im. If he takes Gauru at any point,<b> or<br /> falls into Kuruth while already in Gauru form</b> (such as by taking<br /> Gauru outside of combat), <b>he immediately enters Basu-Im</b>. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T06:43:17-08:00","id":999715,"title":"","content":"Ah, missed that one. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T21:16:49-08:00","id":1000130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=999496#post999496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the rules are pretty clear on that, they shouldn't feel cheated if they've read them. The only way to break out of it is to get an Exceptional Success. Plus there's external abilities that assist these rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring to what I understood as Charlaquin's suggestion of doing a couple rolls and then not rolling anymore. As written in the book, players may keep rolling until they either:<br /> <br /> <b>Fail</b> - At which point they enter Basu-Im.<br /> <b>Succeed</b> - At which point they get some turns without needing to destroy something.<br /> <b>Succeed Exceptionally</b> - At which pont they are free from Kuruth.<br /> <b>Reach the Harmony Limit</b> - At which point they enter Basu-Im.<br /> <br /> It seems that the intention is to build up a scene where the Uratha is desperately fighting against his rage, until he can't hold anymore and loses it. It will work for extreme Harmony characters, because 1 Turn or 10 Turns of Resolve+Composure tests are fast to narrate and might work like combat. However, when you enter the realm of 5 to 15 minutes, rolling each turn is a pretty bad way of representing the action. Centered Harmony Uratha seem much more suited to extended tests, which are made to resume the action encompassing those minutes, like Chases, Investigations and Social Maneuvers. The system just breaks down when characters approach Harmony 5, as it allows, as written, hundreds of tests... It is like asking a player to roll for a 10 minute Speech each time his character finishes a sentence.<br /> <br /> If I just remove several rolls from them to make the scene quicker as Charlaquin suggested, I will be house-ruling it anyway. Better to spend some time on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=999496#post999496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chain Rage allows members of a pack to snap out of Wasu-Im if they make five turns of lucidity. Still Small Voice can be used on others in Wasu-Im to help them break out of it. The Controlled Burn Merit allows you to break out of it with a turn of lucidity and a Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to have not expressed my self clearly, sorry for that. I have no problem with how often Uratha risk Kuruth, and I like it! I just don't feel the mechanics, as described in the book, do a good job portraying the intended mood on <i>Resisting Kuruth Scenes.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=999496#post999496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With your alternative idea, there's far less tension about the rage in general. It might be appropriate for games where people want to cut it out entirely. And attacking the source doesn't really fit, as the source is not always a tangible thing one can attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree on the tension! My experience using conditions is that they are very good for applying feeling to the scene, and with a system like that, I'm just applying a &quot;Wasu-Im&quot; condition on the player, and allowing for beats to come! Balance aside (which I might have done wrong), it does everything that is needed for the mood. It provides a way to resolve the situation with a single roll, to avoid dragging the game down. It allows for all the intended possible scenes, and also can be modified by situations that influence the characters. I don't believe tension is added by a ton of rolls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=999496#post999496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And attacking the source doesn't really fit, as the source is not always a tangible thing one can attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, which mean that if you fail the test, you will certainly enter Basu-Im on those cases. Also, that's why it has the added component of really messing up any social interactions, and I would even add that the player may chose to fail those actions on purpose to earn Beats. An Uratha isolated somewhere resisting Death Rage isn't a very dramatic scene anyway, since he already got far from any possible victims. The focus here is this:<br /> <br /> You get a single roll that sets to mood for the scene, and then you enter a condition based on that roll. The tension comes from being in one of those conditions and near people you don't want to hurt. As I wrote earlier:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> Instantly enter Basu-Im, going straight for the source of the trigger. Even after Basu-Im ends, you suffer from the Atavism condition towards any sources of the same trigger.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> Enter Wasu-Im, suffering from the same Rage limitations from Gauru. After the Harmony timer expires, you enter Basu-Im.<br /> <b>Success:</b> Enter Wasu-Im, but do not suffer the Rage limitations from Gauru. However, each turn in the presence of the trigger forces a Resolve+Composure roll. On a failure on this roll, make when attack against the source. Willpower may be spent to avoid the attack automatically. If your character takes measures to avoid the trigger, he does not need to roll. Also, you react poorly to social interactions. Make the same Resolve+Composure roll whenever someone tries to interact with you, attacking once on a failure. After the Harmony timer expires, you enter Basu-Im.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> You lose the turn, but snap out of Wasu-Im an cannot suffer a Kuruth Trigger Reaction from the same trigger for the scene. </div> </div> </div>Most characters will succeed, since the test usually has 4 dice + willpower. So, most of the time, this will result in a tense scene where the Uratha needs to hold his rage while getting away from everyone, while possibly hurting people in the process. All this without the need to keep on rolling several times. When the rare Exceptional Success appears, they resist fully. And otherwise they suffer similar fates to a player that has failed one of those dozens of Resolve+Composure rolls that would be required in a scene by default.<br /> <br /> Again, I might be wrong with those modifiers and the applied conditions, but the concept is what matters: Allowing for the same intention without the needless rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5446,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","user":"BinAly","date":". 11-08-2016, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T10:18:06-08:00","id":1000314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=1000130#post1000130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was referring to what I understood as Charlaquin's suggestion of doing a couple rolls and then not rolling anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a pretty significant oversimplification of what I was saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=1000130#post1000130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As written in the book, players may keep rolling until they either:<br /> <br /> <b>Fail</b> - At which point they enter Basu-Im.<br /> <b>Succeed</b> - At which point they get some turns without needing to destroy something.<br /> <b>Succeed Exceptionally</b> - At which pont they are free from Kuruth.<br /> <b>Reach the Harmony Limit</b> - At which point they enter Basu-Im.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. But, there are two other conditions under which you stop asking for rolls:<br /> <br /> <b>The Outcome Ceases to be Uncertain</b> - At which point you narrate the only possible result<br /> <b>The Action Ceases to have Dramatic Consequences</b> - At which point you adjudicate a result and move on with the story.<br /> <br /> It's not written that way explicitly in the text, because it's adjudication 101 and a fundamental skill every GM is expected to know. To be fair, I think a lot more RPGs could benefit from explicitly teaching these things to new GMs who might be reading.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=1000130#post1000130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems that the intention is to build up a scene where the Uratha is desperately fighting against his rage, until he can't hold anymore and loses it. It will work for extreme Harmony characters, because 1 Turn or 10 Turns of Resolve+Composure tests are fast to narrate and might work like combat. However, when you enter the realm of 5 to 15 minutes, rolling each turn is a pretty bad way of representing the action. Centered Harmony Uratha seem much more suited to extended tests, which are made to resume the action encompassing those minutes, like Chases, Investigations and Social Maneuvers. The system just breaks down when characters approach Harmony 5, as it allows, as written, hundreds of tests... It is like asking a player to roll for a 10 minute Speech each time his character finishes a sentence.<br /> <br /> If I just remove several rolls from them to make the scene quicker as Charlaquin suggested, I will be house-ruling it anyway. Better to spend some time on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it would help if I gave an example of what I'm suggesting.<br /> <br /> <b>Storyteller:</b> As the silver blade tears into your skin, the sting of your bane sears your soul just as it cleaves into your flesh. The pain awakens something in you, the fight or flight instincts kick in, and you begin to fall into the throes of Wasu-Im. What do you do?<br /> <b>Player:</b> What are my options again?<br /> <b>Storyteller:</b> You can attack the nearest active target, move towards the nearest target if you can't reach them, or roll Resolve + Composure to try to gain one turn of lucidity per success. Anything else will trigger a Reflexive Resolve + Composure roll, and failure on either roll will trigger Bassu-Im.<br /> <b>Player:</b> Ok, I guess I'll try to pull myself together.<br /> <b>Storyteller:</b> Let's see that sweet, sweet Resolve + Composure roll.<br /> <b>Player: </b>Come on, exceptional success! Big bucks, no whammies... *Rolls 4 successes* Damn, just missed it.<br /> <b>Storyteller:</b> How far can you run in four turns?<br /> <b>Player: </b>Let's see, in this form... I've got 17 speed, so 34 meters per turn if I use my action to run... Times four turns, that's... 136 meters.<br /> <b>Storyteller:</b> Alright, that's enough to get you pretty far from the fight. And there are animals out here that will probably be closer than the fight, so at that point it's pretty unlikely your instincts will drive you back to the fray.<br /> <b>Player:</b> That sounds better than sticking around the fight in Basu-Im, at least.<br /> <b>Storyteller:</b> Sounds good. With some effort, you tear yourself back to your senses, if only for a few brief moments.<br /> <br /> At that point, the Storyteller continues to resolve the combat in progress, making sure to double-check with the player each round if they still plan to keep running as far from the fight as possible. At the end of those four turns, the storyteller can cross the character's name off the initiative roster. Whether the player exceptionally succeeds during those 15 minutes or not doesn't make a practical difference to the story at this point, so there's no need to continue rolling dice. Either way, he's out of the fight and off in the woods somewhere. After the fight, the storyteller could even ask the player if they were able to pull themselves out of it or fell to Basu-Im, the latter potentially refilling their Willpower for their Blood Archetype, but giving the Storyteller an opportunity to introduce story complications caused by the player's Death Rage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-08-2016, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T13:31:37-08:00","id":1000410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=1000314#post1000314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip for brevity</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats the way i understood it too. As 2 rolls.<br /> <br /> Player is triggered so he get 4 options.<br /> <br /> 1) Attack.<br /> <br /> 2) Move to attack.<br /> <br /> 3) Roll composure + resolve as an instant action to gain turns to gain breathing room.<br /> <br /> 4) Roll composure + resolve as reflexive action to stay but do something else normally combat related, say arm a trebuchet to attack. Extreme example but you get my meaning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T17:42:11-08:00","id":1000548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=1000314#post1000314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a pretty significant oversimplification of what I was saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry about that, it was not meant to be offensive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=1000314#post1000314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct. But, there are two other conditions under which you stop asking for rolls:<br /> <br /> <b>The Outcome Ceases to be Uncertain</b> - At which point you narrate the only possible result<br /> <b>The Action Ceases to have Dramatic Consequences</b> - At which point you adjudicate a result and move on with the story.<br /> <br /> It's not written that way explicitly in the text, because it's adjudication 101 and a fundamental skill every GM is expected to know. To be fair, I think a lot more RPGs could benefit from explicitly teaching these things to new GMs who might be reading.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is my whole point. That paragraph about Wasu-Im is confusing, at best, and the system doesn't help Storytellers handle the situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998515-questions-about-wasu-im?p=1000314#post1000314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it would help if I gave an example of what I'm suggesting.<br /> <br /> <b>Storyteller:</b> As the silver blade tears into your skin, the sting of your bane sears your soul just as it cleaves into your flesh. The pain awakens something in you, the fight or flight instincts kick in, and you begin to fall into the throes of Wasu-Im. What do you do?<br /> <b>Player:</b> What are my options again?<br /> <b>Storyteller:</b> You can attack the nearest active target, move towards the nearest target if you can't reach them, or roll Resolve + Composure to try to gain one turn of lucidity per success. Anything else will trigger a Reflexive Resolve + Composure roll, and failure on either roll will trigger Bassu-Im.<br /> <b>Player:</b> Ok, I guess I'll try to pull myself together.<br /> <b>Storyteller:</b> Let's see that sweet, sweet Resolve + Composure roll.<br /> <b>Player: </b>Come on, exceptional success! Big bucks, no whammies... *Rolls 4 successes* Damn, just missed it.<br /> <b>Storyteller:</b> How far can you run in four turns?<br /> <b>Player: </b>Let's see, in this form... I've got 17 speed, so 34 meters per turn if I use my action to run... Times four turns, that's... 136 meters.<br /> <b>Storyteller:</b> Alright, that's enough to get you pretty far from the fight. And there are animals out here that will probably be closer than the fight, so at that point it's pretty unlikely your instincts will drive you back to the fray.<br /> <b>Player:</b> That sounds better than sticking around the fight in Basu-Im, at least.<br /> <b>Storyteller:</b> Sounds good. With some effort, you tear yourself back to your senses, if only for a few brief moments.<br /> <br /> At that point, the Storyteller continues to resolve the combat in progress, making sure to double-check with the player each round if they still plan to keep running as far from the fight as possible. At the end of those four turns, the storyteller can cross the character's name off the initiative roster. Whether the player exceptionally succeeds during those 15 minutes or not doesn't make a practical difference to the story at this point, so there's no need to continue rolling dice. Either way, he's out of the fight and off in the woods somewhere. After the fight, the storyteller could even ask the player if they were able to pull themselves out of it or fell to Basu-Im, the latter potentially refilling their Willpower for their Blood Archetype, but giving the Storyteller an opportunity to introduce story complications caused by the player's Death Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>And why not, then, resolve everything with a more relevant single dice-roll? That's exactly what you did there, the only difference from what I proposed is that the outcomes are decided by the dice, not the Storyteller and the Player. I'm fine with simply stating how the story unfolds, but sometimes you want the characters attributes to handle the situation, and for those times, the system as written is lacking.<br /> <br /> And It could get more complicated than that. For example, I'm narrating a chronicle in Chicago, and there are Kuruth situations that a Werewolf can't avoid in 15 minutes running by feet, he will end up killing people anywhere he rans to. Then, discovering if his character resisted or not is far more important to the story. A more robust system to help both storyteller and player handle the outcome in that case would be very nice.<br /> <br /> My whole point is that what is written in that paragraph is confusing, which seems right since every user on this thread got a different understanding on how that should work, even one of the writers. Wasu-Im is a very integral part of playing Werewolf, and reading those rules again, I feel it needs a bit more love, something like the specific Satiety conditions Beasts have, helping them role-play and get beats through it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}